    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a polarized slate today, anchored by a high-upside core. **Kyle Tucker** (80.56) stands as our premier start, benefiting from a favorable matchup against V\u00e1squez and a significant boost from wind conditions, which play right into his elite profile. He is joined in the top tier by **Andy Pages** (72.97) and **Jackson Merrill** (70.60). **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly strong play; despite a moderate SP_xERA, he benefits from a 100% stolen base delivery profile from the opposing pitcher and significant platoon advantages, making him a critical engine for our scarcity-weighted scoring. **Sam Antonacci** (65.19) also earns a strong recommendation, leveraging a prime lead-off spot against a favorable Cecconi matchup.\n\nWhile we are maximizing our scoring potential, the bench remains disciplined. The most difficult cut of the day was **Nolan Schanuel** (39.91), who missed the start by the narrowest of margins. While he possesses solid base projections, the brutal matchup against Miller, whose 2.42 xERA acts as a massive anchor on his score, combined with our strict floor policy, forced him to the bench. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Josh Lowe** (43.62); despite his elite speed, the combination of a difficult opposing pitcher and a low batting order position makes him a marginal play today. We will rely on our top-tier hitters to carry the weight while avoiding the trap of chasing points against high-tier arms. \n\nFinally, a note of caution: we are navigating a \"wait and see\" approach with our roster depth. While **Jordan Westburg** remains sidelined on the IL, our active lineup is optimized for efficiency. Keep a close eye on the weather and late-scratch potential for our middle-of-the-order bats like **Dominic Smith** (48.09) and **Brayan Rocchio** (41.85); both hover near our efficiency floor and will need to capitalize on their respective matchups to provide value above the replacement level. If weather conditions shift the wind or park factors, we are prepared to shift our focus toward our bench depth in the coming days.",
